From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:58:32 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] mozbuild: relpath across drives gives the absolute path

With the objdir on a VRAM disk (R:) and the source on C:, the build's
os.path.relpath calls that make a source path relative to the objdir or the
current directory raise ValueError (gfx/layers/d3d11/genshaders.py was the
first). There is no relative path between drives; the absolute one names the
same file. Patched once in the mozbuild package, which mach and the build's
Python actions all import.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 python/mozbuild/mozbuild/__init__.py | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/__init__.py b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/__init__.py
index e69de29bb2..b8792966e9 100644
--- a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/__init__.py
+++ b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/__init__.py
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
+# License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
+# file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
+
+import os
+import sys
+
+# GeckoW10m: the objdir may be on another drive than the source tree (a VRAM
+# disk at R:, the source on C:). The build runs in the objdir, and the many
+# os.path.relpath calls that make a source path relative -- to the current
+# directory or to the objdir -- raise ValueError across drives on Windows.
+# There is no relative path between two drives; the absolute one names the
+# same file, so that is what they get. Everything that imports mozbuild, mach
+# and the build's Python actions included, is covered.
+if sys.platform == "win32" and not getattr(os.path, "_gecko_w10m_relpath", None):
+    _relpath = os.path.relpath
+
+    def _gecko_w10m_relpath(path, start=None):
+        try:
+            return _relpath(path, start)
+        except ValueError:
+            if os.path.splitdrive(os.path.abspath(path))[0].lower() == (
+                os.path.splitdrive(os.path.abspath(start or os.curdir))[0].lower()
+            ):
+                raise
+            return os.path.abspath(path)
+
+    os.path.relpath = _gecko_w10m_relpath
+    os.path._gecko_w10m_relpath = _relpath
